      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Confirm where you are</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"grep 'You are on' README.md"} lang="bash" />
      <p>The command prints the "You are on" line for stage 00:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"You are on stage 00: setup."} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="open-the-project-in-the-editor" class="group scroll-mt-20">Open the project in the editor<a href="#open-the-project-in-the-editor" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>For the authoring workflow, stage 00 creates a separate <code>audacity-guide</code> repository. Open that folder after creating it. Keep the clone as a reference. For the inspection workflow, open the clone directly.</p>
      <p>If you use the DogsBay XML editor, open the selected folder as a project. The <code>.dogsbay/config.xml</code> on every stage branch sets the project type to DITA, the framework to DITA-OT 4.3.5 and the format style, so the editor and the command line agree on what a valid, well-formatted file is.</p>
      <h2 id="check-the-tools" class="group scroll-mt-20">Check the tools<a href="#check-the-tools" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
